+
+#. Help text for setting "Maximum bit depth" of label #36933
+#: system/settings/linux.xml
+#: system/settings/freebsd.xml
+msgctxt "#36934"
+msgid "Most bits per colour component that the graphics driver may use for the display. \"Auto\" leaves the driver default, which some drivers keep at 8 bit. Choose at least 10 bit to show 10 bit video without reducing it to 8 bit. The driver lowers the depth by itself when the display or the video mode cannot carry it, and with \"Adaptive\" colour format a limit of 8 bit turns the switch to YCbCr off."
+msgstr ""
